{"cluster_id": "C-2224", "topic": "Any operation that changes committed root.refs or committed", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B039-053", "B039-054", "B039-065"], "canonical_claim": "Any operation that changes committed `root.refs` or committed `RootRef::mutable_files` must be a method on `CachedPartFolderAccess`. `ContentAddressedTransaction` committed part-reference mutations must replace raw `Store::dropRef`, raw `Store::updateRefPublishedAt`, direct final `Build::promote`, and table/shadow namespace drops with facade calls.; The final committed owner mutation may use `Cas::Build` for staging, blob upload, evidence adoption, and precommit, but the mutation itself must go through the facade.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/cache.md#contentaddressedtransaction", "docs/superpowers/cas/cache.md#write-flow"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2225", "topic": "Build::stageManifest writes manifest bodies with putIfAbsentStream, ManifestId is", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B039-075", "B040-087"], "canonical_claim": "`Build::stageManifest` writes manifest bodies with `putIfAbsentStream`, `ManifestId` is namespace-qualified and freshly minted, and `readManifest` validates `RefMatchesBody` and `ManifestNamespaceMatches`. Store::readManifest checks that the journal ManifestRef matches the decoded part-manifest body and that the decoded namespace matches the owning namespace", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/cache.md#manifest-body-risks", "docs/superpowers/cas/codecs.md#part-manifest-capt"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2226", "topic": "The per-namespace life_epoch design is not executable because", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B040-066", "B040-072"], "canonical_claim": "The per-namespace life_epoch design is not executable because the plan retains validateEpochSealGrammar(const RefLogTxn &) and does not propagate life_epoch through encodeRefLogTxn, decodeRefLogTxn, and their callers The plan still prescribes the stale validateEpochSealGrammar API in its Grammar paragraph, Step 3, and Task 6 Consumes block despite intending a structural/contextual split", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_plans_r3_findings.md#L4-L5", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_plans_r4_findings.md#L3-L3"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2227", "topic": "A valid successor EpochSeal occupying a ref slot", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B027-127", "B041-046"], "canonical_claim": "A valid successor EpochSeal occupying a ref slot is conclusive rejection of the old transaction, not corruption. `resolveWedgeOnce` performs at most one `slotOccupy` under the wedge's original admitted generation: `Created` or matching-byte `Occupied` adopts the operation, an occupied successor `EpochSeal` conclusively rejects it and clears the wedge, a foreign non-seal occupant is `CORRUPTED_DATA`, and `Unresolved` leaves the lane wedged.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-a-streams.md#task-4", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r7_findings.md#L127-L135"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2228", "topic": "planManifestCursorPage may recover debris only for a catalog-named", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B047-035", "B048-002"], "canonical_claim": "`planManifestCursorPage` may recover debris only for a catalog-named namespace when `catalog_recovery_authoritative` is true; it still requires `prefixEligible`, rejects `Creating` state, survives the protection-view try/catch, and checks active keys before nomination. In `planManifestCursorPage`, `catalog_recovery_authoritative` controls only whether debris for a catalog-named namespace may be recovered; recovery still requires `prefixEligible`, refuses `Creating`, handles protection-view exceptions, and checks active keys before nomination.", "issue_ids": ["T6"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6-review-opus.md#L46-L66", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t6-review.md#L41-L49"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2229", "topic": "RefTableSnapshot represents only a live generation-8 snapshot and", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B050-002", "B050-013"], "canonical_claim": "`RefTableSnapshot` represents only a live generation-8 snapshot and has no `lifecycle` or `remove_txn_id` member. The final `RefTableSnapshot` contains only `ns`, `snapshot_id`, committed rows, and precommits.", "issue_ids": ["T5"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/task-5-step9-c-brief.md#L8-L8", ".superpowers/sdd/task-5-step9-c-report.md#L19-L20"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2230", "topic": "Ref transaction IDs contain nonzero writer_epoch and ref_sequence", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B004-060", "B012-021"], "canonical_claim": "Ref transaction IDs contain nonzero `writer_epoch` and `ref_sequence`; `renderRefTxnId` renders canonical IDs as `0000000000000007-000000000000008e`, and `parseRefTxnId` accepts only the canonical form. Ref transaction ids are per-namespace contiguous pairs `(writer_epoch, ref_sequence)` rendered as fixed-width hexadecimal fields; `applyRefLogTxn` rejects a non-successor id with `CORRUPTED_DATA`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/11-walkthrough.md#in-s3", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-phase1.md#L69-L75"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2231", "topic": "Ref snapshot encoding requires committed and precommit inputs", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B012-026", "B017-013"], "canonical_claim": "Ref snapshot encoding requires committed and precommit inputs to be sorted and rejects unsorted or duplicate rows; a `Removed` snapshot must have zero rows and a `remove_txn_id`. Snapshot committed rows are strictly ascending by `ref_name`, precommits are strictly ascending by `(ref_name, manifest_ref)`, and every precommit has `kind == Precommit`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-phase1.md#L236-L246", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-codecs-v3-phase3-refsnaplog.md#global-constraints"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2232", "topic": "Publish-from-live copies rt->state exactly once under state_mutex at", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B014-076", "B015-026", "B015-036"], "canonical_claim": "Publish-from-live copies `rt->state` exactly once under `state_mutex` at a transaction boundary, encodes and conditionally writes outside the lock, and adopts the result by subtracting captured tail counters instead of replaying `snapshot_base_state` plus `tail_since_snapshot`. Snapshot publication copies the live state once at a transaction boundary when the count threshold exceeds `snapshot_log_count_threshold` or the bytes threshold fires, then encodes and PUTs asynchronously. The proposal raised `snapshot_log_count_threshold` from 64 to 256 and replaced grace-window replay with copy-once-from-live publication.", "issue_ids": ["rev.6"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-13-cas-ref-lease-exclusivity-rev6.md#task-10", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-13-cas-ref-lease-exclusivity-rev6-design.md#ref-simplification", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-13-cas-ref-lease-exclusivity-rev6-proposal.md#publish-from-live"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2233", "topic": "P3 was a recurring stageManifest: manifest ordinal collision", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B007-020"], "canonical_claim": "P3 was a recurring `stageManifest: manifest ordinal collision`; one instance escaped retry to a foreground query as `LOGICAL_ERROR` 28 seconds after ch1 was mount-fenced.", "issue_ids": ["P3"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-06-cas-night-findings-fix-plan-design.md#re-audit"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2234", "topic": "A content-static ref-shard can permanently orphan a manifest", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B007-069"], "canonical_claim": "A content-static ref-shard can permanently orphan a manifest when an abandoned precommit remains in its journal: token-diff `Skip` prevents `reclaimAbandonedPrecommit` from running after the watermark later proves the precommit dead.", "issue_ids": ["S30"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-07-cas-dangling-precommit-manifest-orphan-fix-design.md#mechanism-of-the-leak"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2235", "topic": "Using raw tail_since_snapshot.size() > 64 for maybeScheduleSnapshotPublish causes", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B014-014"], "canonical_claim": "Using raw `tail_since_snapshot.size() > 64` for `maybeScheduleSnapshotPublish` causes continuous snapshot publishing under sustained load because the 5-second grace window alone leaves roughly 115\u2013230 young entries in the tail at combined append rates of 23\u201346 entries per second.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-12-unattended-refsnaplog-stabilization.md#L208-L226"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2236", "topic": "trySnapshotPublishOnce copied the full RefTableState once per aged", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B014-016"], "canonical_claim": "`trySnapshotPublishOnce` copied the full `RefTableState` once per aged tail entry at `CasStore.cpp:1985`, and the replay-plus-copy loop held `rt->state_mutex`, blocking concurrent `flushRefBatch` admissions for its duration.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-12-unattended-refsnaplog-stabilization.md#L208-L226"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2237", "topic": "A late predecessor log cannot enter the live", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B014-018"], "canonical_claim": "A late predecessor log cannot enter the live ref state because `applyRefLogTxn` requires a strict increase over `greatest_applied`; it also does not enter `tail_since_snapshot` without a steady-state re-list, so it is visible only to cold folds during a race-dependent divergent-observer window before a covering snapshot and then becomes permanently invisible.", "issue_ids": ["rev.6"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-12-unattended-refsnaplog-stabilization.md#L242-L260"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2238", "topic": "WriterPublishSnapshot must use CoveredFold, which excludes droppedEver under", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B014-064"], "canonical_claim": "`WriterPublishSnapshot` must use `CoveredFold`, which excludes `droppedEver` under `Rev6MountRule`; otherwise a later snapshot can silently re-include a dropped id and make `INV_SNAP_DETERMINISTIC` unsatisfiable.", "issue_ids": ["rev.6"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-13-cas-ref-lease-exclusivity-rev6.md#task-1-amendment"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2239", "topic": "Without a MOVING_DIR_NAME parser case, every file under", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B019-019"], "canonical_claim": "Without a `MOVING_DIR_NAME` parser case, every file under `<table>/moving/<part>/` routes to the literal ref `moving`, causing all files and all moved parts to collide.", "issue_ids": ["S36"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-17-cas-move-to-ca-design.md#L10-L12"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2240", "topic": "RefTableState has accumulated keyed lookup, ordered canonical scans", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B022-073"], "canonical_claim": "`RefTableState` has accumulated keyed lookup, ordered canonical scans, cheap snapshots, batch apply, incremental byte accounting, manifest-owner uniqueness, and mass replay while remaining a mutable struct whose derived fields can be bypassed by direct mutation.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-21-reftablestate-closed-class-experiments-design.md#problem"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2241", "topic": "Using std::unordered_map for the RefCowManifestSet overlay increased scratch-copy", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B023-021"], "canonical_claim": "Using `std::unordered_map` for the `RefCowManifestSet` overlay increased scratch-copy cost by 37% to 42% because copying an empty unordered map allocates a bucket array; the overlay was changed to `std::map`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-21-reftablestate-experiments.md#e2-scratchcopy-investigation"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2242", "topic": "Snapshot publication must re-evaluate the accumulated tail or", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B024-019"], "canonical_claim": "Snapshot publication must re-evaluate the accumulated tail or remember and re-fire a pending trigger, because single-flight suppression can otherwise let a publication of chunk 1 hide chunks 2 through N indefinitely.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-22-cas-writepath-stage1-internal-design.md#budget"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2243", "topic": "A ref-log transaction can become durable before its", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B024-037"], "canonical_claim": "A ref-log transaction can become durable before its in-memory apply throws, allowing a later transaction to apply without contiguity checking and a snapshot to label the state with the later transaction id, permanently hiding the earlier transaction from recovery.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-23-cas-fetch-handoff-publish-confirm-design.md#problem-ledger"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2244", "topic": "The stage-1 ref-lane leader originally published leader_active =", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B025-040"], "canonical_claim": "The stage-1 ref-lane leader originally published `leader_active = true` before allocating its first responsibility entry, so an allocation exception could strand the leadership baton and block later appends indefinitely.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-24-codex-stage1-reviews.md#round-1"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2245", "topic": "A publish appends both precommitAdd and promote ref-log", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B026-003"], "canonical_claim": "A publish appends both `precommitAdd` and `promote` ref-log transactions; `precommitAdd` carries the activation `+1` edge, while `promote` moves the owner at the same `manifest_ref` and emits no edge.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-25-cas-followups-detector-introspection-s42-forceclaim.md#task-1-the-mirror-safety-test-make-the-deletion-path-executable-expect-red"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2246", "topic": "Because read-created catalog entries are not reclaimed, reads", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B028-065"], "canonical_claim": "Because read-created catalog entries are not reclaimed, reads against nonexistent tables can grow the one pool-wide catalog without bound and exhaust admission capacity for legitimate creations.", "issue_ids": ["R12"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/2026-07-28-ref-rework-adjacent-findings.md#r12-read-births-namespace"]}
