{"cluster_id": "C-2248", "topic": "Concurrent verbatim append can lose updates because CAS", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B033-105"], "canonical_claim": "Concurrent verbatim append can lose updates because CAS retry reuses stale `old + suffix` data instead of rereading the winner's value; the path is used for mutation-entry CSN append.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/20260717_codex_review.md#major-severity"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2249", "topic": "Pool::beginPartWrite has an allocate/register window in which a", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B034-031"], "canonical_claim": "`Pool::beginPartWrite` has an allocate/register window in which a build can be allocated after a drop sweep snapshots `inflight_builds`, reviving an empty ownerless `Live` namespace that GC does not sweep.", "issue_ids": ["codex-11"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/BACKLOG.md#gc-followups"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2250", "topic": "A damaged _ckpt is isolated to a per-namespace", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B034-079"], "canonical_claim": "A damaged `_ckpt` is isolated to a per-namespace hold, but that hold still shuts the round-wide destructive gate and `publishCkpt` has no repair path because it hits the same decode failure.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/BACKLOG.md#ckpt-damage-no-repair-path"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2251", "topic": "The catalog's single-object atomicity makes every table creation", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B034-117"], "canonical_claim": "The catalog's single-object atomicity makes every table creation contend on the same CAS target, turning high-rate table creation into timeout-prone serialization; reverting to unreliable pool LIST is not the accepted fix direction.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/BACKLOG.md#ref-catalog-write-hotspot"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2252", "topic": "The strict sequence-1 grammar requiring prev_epoch_seal on every", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B040-018", "B041-029"], "canonical_claim": "The strict sequence-1 grammar requiring prev_epoch_seal on every non-genesis epoch is unusable because the ordinary {E,1} append path does not copy the recovered predecessor seal; An EpochSeal transaction must contain exactly one seal operation, no manifest edges or lifecycle changes, and prev_epoch_seal exactly on sequence 1 of every non-genesis epoch, including a sequence-1 seal.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_plans_r1_findings.md#L4-L6", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r6_findings.md#L104-L110"]}
